# Qguard Helix — Deep Technical Audit, Data Integrity Validation, and Enterprise UI/UX Enhancement

## Objective

Perform a comprehensive, end-to-end technical audit, validation, and improvement of the following seven Qguard Helix dashboard modules. Verify that every page is correctly integrated with the actual backend, database, APIs, hooks, Server-Sent Events (SSE), real-time event streams, and other relevant data sources.

The primary objective is to ensure that all displayed metrics, asset inventories, statuses, findings, workflows, risk scores, migration progress, and recommendations accurately reflect the user's **actual assets, real system state, and verified operational events**.

After completing the technical audit, improve each module's visual presentation, workflow representation, usability, and customer experience to achieve a polished, premium, modern, and enterprise-grade cybersecurity platform.

**Important:** Do not merely redesign the frontend. Investigate, validate, repair, and test the complete data flow from the source of truth to the backend, frontend hooks, real-time updates, calculations, and final UI rendering.

