## Final Instruction

Begin by inspecting the existing codebase, architecture, shared services, database schema, API routes, hooks, event mechanisms, and all seven pages. Establish the actual source of truth before changing the implementation.

Proceed systematically: **audit → identify root causes → implement fixes → improve visualizations → test → verify → report**.

Prioritize data correctness, security, functional reliability, and operational transparency before visual polish.

The final result should be a genuinely functional, data-driven, real-time-capable Qguard Helix platform in which customers can trust the displayed asset information, understand the security implications, follow workflows easily, and take informed action.

Do not stop after producing recommendations. Implement the verified improvements directly in the existing codebase where feasible, preserve working functionality, and provide an evidence-based report of the actual results.